INVENTORY & STAFF TASK MANAGEMENT SYSTEM
Software requirements | Web-based, multi-user application
Build one cloud-based system for tracking stock quantities and exact warehouse locations, assigning staff
tasks and schedules, and reviewing proof of completion. It must work in Google Chrome on desktop, tablet,
Android, and iPhone, with simultaneous access and individual password-protected accounts.
1 Roles and permissions
Admin / authorized supervisor
• Manage users, items, warehouses and storage locations; receive, release, transfer and correct stock.
• Assign tasks and schedules; monitor all employees; review uploaded evidence; approve or return submitted tasks.
• Access reports, exports and the activity log. Supervisors may receive a narrower permission set configured by Admin.
Staff
• View only their own assigned tasks, instructions and schedule.
• Submit completion remarks and upload photos, delivery receipts, receiving records or other evidence.
• Cannot assign tasks, alter the original instructions, delete records or change inventory unless specifically granted
permission.
2 Inventory and warehouse
Item master list
• Item code/SKU, name, category, description, unit of measurement, supplier, minimum stock threshold, active/inactive
status and date created.
• Show current available quantity by item and by exact warehouse location; optionally show cost and inventory value.
• Maintain stock as a transaction-based balance: opening balance + stock in - stock out +/- adjustments. Transfers change
location balances without changing total stock.
Stock in
Record date, item, quantity, unit, supplier, purchase order/reference, delivery receipt number, warehouse, exact storage
location, receiver, remarks and attachments. Increase stock only after the receipt is confirmed.
Stock out
Record date, item, quantity, unit, source warehouse and location, recipient/customer/department, purpose, delivery receipt,
releasing and receiving persons, remarks and attachments. Decrease stock only after confirmation. Block a withdrawal
exceeding available stock unless Admin explicitly authorizes a controlled exception.
Warehouses, locations and transfers
Support multiple warehouses and nested locations (for example, Biaan Warehouse / Freezer 2 / Rack B). Search an item to
see item, quantity, warehouse and exact location. Record internal transfers with source and destination, quantity, time, user
and reference; prevent the transfer from being counted as a sale.
Movement history and dashboard
• Every movement records date/time, type, quantity change, running balance, location, reference and user. Preserve
original transactions when making corrections.
• Admin dashboard: total SKUs, stock on hand, optional value, receipts and releases today, low/out-of-stock items, recent
movements, totals by warehouse/category, and item/location search.
