3 Staff tasks and schedules
Staff directory and task assignment
Maintain employee name, role, position, department, contact number, username, account status and optional photo. Only
Admin or an authorized supervisor can create tasks. Each task has an ID, title, instructions, assignee, assignment and due
date/time, work location, priority, status, attachments and remarks.
Priority: Low, Normal, High, Urgent. Workflow: Not Started → In Progress → For Verification → Completed. The Admin may
also Cancel a task or return it as Needs Correction.
Schedule calendar
Show daily, weekly and monthly views. Admin can see all staff and filter by employee; each staff member sees only their
own schedule. Tasks display start time, due time, location and status. For example: Sept. 28 — Juan: 8:00 receive delivery;
10:00 inventory count; 2:00 deliver items.
Proof and verification
• Staff may add completion remarks and upload a work photo, delivery receipt, receiving document or other supporting file.
Record uploader, task, date and time.
• Submission moves a task to For Verification. Admin approves it as Completed or returns it as Needs Correction with a
reason. Preserve the submission and review history.
Task dashboard and notifications
Admin sees counts by status and employee, overdue and due-today tasks, and items awaiting verification. In-app
notifications cover new assignments, due and overdue tasks, returned and approved work, and low or out-of-stock items.
4 Reports and exports
• Inventory: receipts, releases, current stock, stock by warehouse/location, movement history, low stock and per-item
history.
• Staff: assigned/completed/pending/overdue tasks, tasks by employee/date/location, and employee activity.
• Provide date-range filters, search and Excel / Print gusto ko parang mag nenew tab siya tapos simpleng printing lang ang gusto ko makita hindi yung madaming design kung ano lang ang need
5 Security and technical requirements
• Individual login accounts with password protection and server-enforced role-based permissions. Staff must not access
another employee’s private tasks or documents by changing a URL.
• Centralized database and file storage, responsive Chrome interface, and safe simultaneous use without lost updates or
double stock deductions.
• Audit log with date/time, user and action for login, stock transactions and corrections, task assignments, uploads, review
decisions and edits. Keep history instead of permanently deleting important transactions.
• Support practical backup/restore and validation of uploaded file types and sizes.
Acceptance checks
• Receive an item into one rack, transfer part to another rack, and release part: the total and each location balance update
correctly.
• Two users attempt to release the same limited stock at once: the system prevents an invalid balance.
• A staff member sees their own schedule and submits a delivery receipt; Admin can approve or return it; another staff
member cannot access it.
• Admin can filter and export inventory and staff reports, with the actions visible in the audit history